# project: product-localization
// Localize the product into six languages: glossary freeze, per-language
// vendor pipeline with reviewer bounce, integration, layout checks, ship.

VAR languages_approved = 0
VAR review_rounds = 0
VAR layout_fix_rounds = 0

-> freeze_glossary

=== freeze_glossary ===
Freeze the source-string glossary so translation starts from a stable base.
Product marketing owns this sign-off; nothing moves until the glossary is locked.
+ [Marketing approves the frozen glossary] @human -> vendor_translation
+ [Glossary needs another revision] @human ~loop~ -> freeze_glossary

=== vendor_translation ===
The translation vendor translates the current language from the frozen glossary.
One language moves through the pipeline at a time; this phase re-enters for each of the six.
~ review_rounds = 0
+ [Translation draft delivered] -> vendor_qa

=== vendor_qa ===
The vendor runs its own QA pass on the translated language before handing it to the in-country reviewer.
+ [Vendor QA passes] -> reviewer_review

=== reviewer_review ===
The in-country reviewer evaluates the language for accuracy, tone and terminology.
The language bounces back to vendor fixes until the reviewer is satisfied.
+ [Reviewer approves this language] @human -> language_approved
+ {review_rounds < 4} [Changes requested] @human ~loop~ -> vendor_fixes
+ {review_rounds >= 4} [Still bouncing after four rounds] -> manager_arbitration

=== vendor_fixes ===
The vendor applies the reviewer's requested fixes to this language.
~ review_rounds += 1
+ [Fixes applied, back to the reviewer] ~loop~ -> reviewer_review

=== manager_arbitration ===
The localization manager arbitrates a language stuck after four review rounds:
accept it as-is, or direct one more targeted fix round.
+ [Manager accepts the language as-is] @human -> language_approved
+ [Manager directs another fix round] @human ~loop~ -> vendor_fixes

=== language_approved ===
This language is approved and banked. Move to the next language, or to
integration once all six are done.
~ languages_approved += 1
+ {languages_approved < 6} [Start the next language] ~loop~ -> vendor_translation
+ {languages_approved >= 6} [All six languages approved] -> integration

=== integration ===
Integrate all six approved languages into the product build.
* [Integration complete] -> layout_checks

=== layout_checks ===
Run pseudo-localization and layout checks across the integrated build,
looking for truncation and overflow bugs.
+ [All layout checks pass] -> ship
+ {layout_fix_rounds < 3} [Truncation or layout bugs found] ~loop~ -> fix_truncation
+ {layout_fix_rounds >= 3} [Still failing after three fix rounds] -> partial_ship_decision

=== fix_truncation ===
Fix the truncation and layout bugs surfaced by the checks.
~ layout_fix_rounds += 1
+ [Fixes applied, re-run the checks] ~loop~ -> layout_checks

=== partial_ship_decision ===
Layout checks are still failing after three fix rounds. The localization
manager decides which passing languages ship now and which are deferred.
+ [Ship the passing languages, defer the rest] @human -> ship
+ [Keep fixing instead] @human ~loop~ -> fix_truncation

=== ship ===
Release the localized product with the approved (or manager-selected) languages.
-> END
